{"name":"Tabbouleh","hex":"#709572","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tabbouleh","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Levantine salad or meze generally consisting of bulgur wheat, chopped tomatoes, parsley, olive oil, and lemon juice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tabbouleh"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tabbouleh","blocks":[{"text":"Tabbouleh, also transcribed tabouleh, tabbouli, tabouli, or taboulah, is a Levantine salad of finely chopped parsley, soaked bulgur, tomatoes, mint, and onion, seasoned with olive oil, lemon juice, salt and sweet pepper. Some variations add lettuce, or use semolina instead of bulgur."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Tabouleh_1.JPG/330px-Tabouleh_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tabbouleh"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Tabouleh_%283949565145%29.jpg/500px-Tabouleh_%283949565145%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Tabouleh_%283949565145%29.jpg/1280px-Tabouleh_%283949565145%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Tabouleh_%283949565145%29.jpg/500px-Tabouleh_%283949565145%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tabbouleh ingredients","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATabouleh_(3949565145).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Oasis_taboule.jpg/500px-Oasis_taboule.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Oasis_taboule.jpg/1280px-Oasis_taboule.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia